0. ROLE AND GOAL

You are a senior Node.js/TypeScript backend engineer. Build the REST API backend for the Oromia Hospitality & Tourism Professionals Association (OHPEA) website and member-management system.

The system replaces the association's manual, unorganized member records with one secure database. It serves two front ends: a public website (with member registration) and an admin portal (member management, statistics, contributions, SMS, content).

Keep the exact architecture, folder layout, coding style and conventions of my previous backend Delta_API (https://github.com/fevensamuel/Delta_API.git). Study it before writing code. Reuse its patterns. Only the domain changes (travel packages become members, contributions and announcements).

0.1 SCOPE: BACKEND ONLY, NO UI OF ANY KIND (hard rules)

This repo is a headless JSON API, exactly like Delta_API. All screens, dashboards, forms, pages and management interfaces live in the separate admin app (Delta_Admin pattern, Prompt 2) and the separate public website (Prompt 3). The backend only exposes data and business logic through endpoints.

The backend must NOT contain, serve or link to:

Any HTML page or template: no landing page at /, no status page, no error pages in HTML (Swagger UI aside), no template engine (ejs, pug, handlebars), no React/Vite/Tailwind, no public/ or views/ folder with pages, no index.html.
Swagger UI is the one exception and MUST be included at /api-docs (same as Delta_API). No other API explorer (no Redoc, no GraphiQL).
No admin panel, dashboard, member management screen or login page served from the backend, and no serving of the admin or public front-end builds (dist/). Each front end is deployed and hosted on its own.
No UI-oriented code: no HTML emails built with a UI framework beyond plain transactional email templates (OTP, receipt, contact notification) rendered as simple strings, and no server-side rendering.
GET / returns only a small JSON object { "success": true, "name": "OHPEA API", "version": "x.y.z" }. GET /health and GET /api/health return JSON. Unknown routes return JSON 404.

"Managing" features (create/edit/approve/delete/export/send SMS and so on) are endpoints only. The screens that call them are built in the admin app. The backend keeps the business rules, validation, permissions, region scoping, audit logging and file generation (Excel/PDF exports and receipts are generated on request and returned as downloads).

Acceptance check before finishing: search the repo (including package.json, dist/, README) for .html, ejs, pug, react, vite, tailwind, express.static and sendFile. Allowed hits: swagger-ui-express and /api-docs (required), express.static only for the UPLOAD_PATH public-images directory, and plain-string email templates. Also confirm /api-docs loads and lists every endpoint. Report the result in your final message.

