6. BUSINESS LOGIC
6.1 Registration flow (public)
(Phase 3, flagged) POST /api/public/registrations/otp/request { email } sends a 6-digit code (hashed in DB, 10-minute TTL, 5 attempts, max 3 requests per email per hour). POST .../otp/verify { email, code } returns a short-lived otpToken (JWT, 15 min) that the registration submit must include. When FEATURE_EMAIL_OTP=false the submit works without a token.
POST /api/public/registrations is multipart/form-data (fields + idDocument x1 + credentials x1-5). Validate with zod, normalize phone, reject invalid files by extension, MIME and magic bytes. On success return { memberNo, status: "pending" } and send a confirmation SMS/email if enabled.
Member lands as registration_status='pending'. It does not appear on public stats until approved.
6.2 Duplicate detection (Phase 2, but build the helper now)

Block or flag when any of these match an existing member: normalized phone, lowercase email, sha256(idType + ':' + normalizedIdNumber + SERVER_PEPPER), or fuzzy name + date of birth. Return a clear 409 with a safe message (do not reveal whose record matched). Admin can see "possible duplicate" flags in the pending list.

6.3 Approval

POST /api/admin/members/:id/approve and /reject (reason required). Regional admins may only act on members in their own region. Both write an audit log and optionally trigger SMS/email.

6.4 Contributions
Admin or Finance records a payment: POST /api/admin/payments. Server computes period_start/period_end from period + paidFor date, generates receipt_no (RCT-2026-000123), copies region_id, and flips the member's membership_status to active if it was pending.
Paid vs unpaid for a period is computed: members with membership_status IN ('active','pending') and no paid payment covering that period.
Members with no payment for N consecutive periods (configurable setting inactive_after_periods, default 2 yearly or 6 monthly) are listed as "at risk"; provide an admin action to bulk-mark inactive. Do not auto-deactivate silently.
GET /api/admin/dashboard/contributions?range=3m|6m|12m&group=week|month|year&regionId= returns time series { bucket, totalEtb, paymentsCount }[], plus totalCollected, paidMembers, unpaidMembers, and a breakdown by period type, region and method. All numbers via SQL SUM/COUNT at query time.
6.5 Statistics (statsService)

GET /api/admin/dashboard/summary returns: totalMembers, active, inactive, pending, pendingRegistrations, female, male, governmentCount, privateCount, otherCount, newThisMonth, totalCollectedThisYear. GET /api/admin/dashboard/members-by?dimension=gender|sector|field|occupation|region|graduationLevel returns [{ key, label, count, percent }] (labels localized by ?lang=). Regional admins are auto-scoped to their region. GET /api/public/stats returns only safe aggregates: approved total, active total, number of regions, number of programs, activities this year. No personal data.

6.6 Roles, permissions and region scope

Same pattern as Delta_API (role + permissions[], SuperAdmin bypasses). Roles:

SuperAdmin: everything, manages admins, lookups, settings, audit logs.
RegionalAdmin: members, registrations, payment view, dashboards only for their region_id (enforced in SQL via requireRegionScope which injects the region into every query, never trusted from the client).
Finance: payments, plans, contribution dashboards, receipts, exports of payment reports; read-only on members.
Editor: announcements, programs, activities, partners, site settings, contact inbox; no member PII.

Permission keys: dashboard, members, members.approve, members.edit, members.export, payments, payments.record, payments.void, contributions.dashboard, announcements, programs, partners, activities, sms, subscribers, messages, regions, lookups, settings.site, settings.contact, translations, audit, plus Phase 4: jobs, b2b, investments, resources, international, region-resources. Expose GET /api/admin/meta/permissions so the admin UI renders the checkboxes from one source of truth.

